 "translation": "Listen, listen! Kishwar's distressed voice came. She was pleading with that wretched man. Then it seemed as if someone was dragging someone by force, and that person was begging, asking for refuge in their death throes. And then an even more muffled voice started coming, as if some powerful beast was mauling Kishwar. My temples began to throb, my nerves tensed up, and my hands stiffened. That moment had arrived. I suddenly stood up. \"Hey, hey, Rehana, what are you doing?\" Rahat stopped me.",
